{
"dur": 57.645,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 4.695,
"text": "Ross William Ulbricht was born in Austin, Texas, in March 1984.",
"end": 4.97
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 4.97,
"vo_start": 5.245,
"vo_end": 10.657,
"text": "He was an Eagle Scout, then a physics student at the University of Texas at Dallas, on a full scholarship.",
"end": 10.932
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 10.932,
"vo_start": 11.207,
"vo_end": 15.367,
"text": "He went on to a master's degree in materials science at Penn State, studying crystals.",
"end": 15.642
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 15.642,
"vo_start": 15.917,
"vo_end": 19.317,
"text": "But along the way he lost interest in science, and fell for an idea.",
"end": 19.592
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 19.592,
"vo_start": 19.867,
"vo_end": 26.589,
"text": "He became a libertarian: someone who believes the government should stay out of people's lives, including what they buy and what they put in their bodies.",
"end": 26.864
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 26.864,
"vo_start": 27.139,
"vo_end": 33.113,
"text": "Back in Austin he tried running small businesses, including a used-book company. None of them took off.",
"end": 33.388
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 33.388,
"vo_start": 33.663,
"vo_end": 40.263,
"text": "Then he had a bigger plan: a hidden online market where people could buy and sell almost anything, behind Tor, paid in Bitcoin.",
"end": 40.538
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 40.538,
"vo_start": 40.813,
"vo_end": 48.732,
"text": "He taught himself to code. His own journal says he grew illegal mushrooms in a cabin, so the site had something to sell on day one.",
"end": 49.007
},
{
"i": 9,
"start": 49.007,
"vo_start": 49.282,
"vo_end": 55.387,
"text": "In early 2011, at twenty-six, he launched it. He named it after the ancient trade route between China and the West.",
"end": 55.662
},
{
"i": 10,
"start": 55.662,
"vo_start": 55.937,
"vo_end": 56.695,
"text": "Silk Road.",
"end": 57.645
}
],
